  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 129 AM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nAs we go into the latter part of the week into the weekend, models \ndiffer on how they handle the upper low, but either solution(GFS or \nEuro) would keep precip chances in the forecast through the end of \nthe week and through the upcoming weekend. Still heavy rainfall \npotential continues Thursday into Friday across south central and \nsoutheast parts of the state.\n\nWith this continuation of rain, associated cloud cover and frontal \npassage that will occur late in the week, temperatures will finally \nbegin to feel more like fall instead of summer. Most areas from \nThursday into at least Saturday will in the 70s and lower 80s. There \nis a chance for a few locations, especially Friday as cooler surface \nhigh pokes south into the area, to see highs only in the 60s.",
